title the aliases both parsers now refuse

# Kept out of the byte-exact cross-parser diff because the two
# parsers word this refusal differently, not because they disagree
# about it.
#
# The reference parser used to ACCEPT "left" and "right", bound the
# opposite way round from the harness -- onto is RT_DS_RIGHT, off-of
# is RT_DS_LEFT -- so a fixture written with them would have mirrored
# silently and still produced a plausible result. It refuses them now
# too, and engine-tests.js P7 guards that.
#
# This parser says WHY, since whoever hits it is writing a fixture
# and the polarity is the fact they need; the reference just calls
# the name unknown. treecheck.sh asserts both refusals, so the claim
# "they differ only in wording" is checked rather than asserted.

tree left
  1-1: /

tree right
  1-1: /
